        summary: 'In HTTP messages, the payload body or payload was the resource representation transferred in a message body, stripped of any transfer encoding. With no transfer encoding, the payload body and message body are identical. Representation data could also be transferred in HTTP headers, but such data would not be considered a "payload".',
