        summary: "Grid systems are a very common feature used in CSS layouts, and before CSS grid layout they tended to be implemented using floats or other layout features. You imagine your layout as a set number of columns (e.g., 4, 6, or 12), and then fit your content columns inside these imaginary columns. In this article we'll explore how these older methods work, in order that you understand how they were used if you work on an older project.",
